  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676036",
      "title": "User Signup & Password Hashing",
      "lectureOrder": 93,
      "videoOrder": 86,
      "sourceHash": "60291026ed77443417c90d8dce6ab21a01055a7a08b94075c9c06680f7a23d18",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 4.68,
          "en": "Let's say we made it past this safe check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.68,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "So we have no user with that email yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 11.64,
          "en": "In that case, we then wanna store that user, that new user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.64,
          "end": 12.693,
          "en": "in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 16.05,
          "en": "For this, we can use Prisma again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.05,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "and they're the user field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 19.5,
          "en": "and call create,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 22.56,
          "en": "set the data field on that configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.56,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "and there simply set the email to our email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 31.88,
          "en": "and the password to our password here, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 36.51,
          "en": "Well, that would really not be good if we did it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.51,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "If we did it like this, we would store the password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 43.02,
          "en": "entered by the user as plain text in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.02,
          "end": 44.61,
          "en": "And you don't wanna do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.61,
          "end": 47.58,
          "en": "because if your database ever gets compromised",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.58,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "all the passwords are stored in plain text there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "And that's definitely not something you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "You should never store user passwords in plain text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 59.91,
          "en": "Instead, it should be hashed first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.91,
          "end": 61.8,
          "en": "So it should be transformed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.8,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "in such a way that it can't be decoded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.25,
          "end": 66.54,
          "en": "And to achieve this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 71.53999999999999,
          "en": "what we'll do is install an extra package called bcrypt js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 75.81,
          "en": "which is a package commonly used for hashing passwords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.81,
          "end": 77.76,
          "en": "So for transforming passwords",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.76,
          "end": 81.813,
          "en": "into something unreadable that can't be transformed back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.82,
          "end": 86.16,
          "en": "And with bcrypt installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.16,
          "end": 91.16,
          "en": "we can use bcrypt by importing from the bcrypt package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 95.07,
          "en": "So from bcrypt js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.07,
          "end": 98.31,
          "en": "and we wanna import the hash function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.31,
          "end": 101.07,
          "en": "which does what the name applies, it hashes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.07,
          "end": 103.023,
          "en": "it converts a password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.46000000000001,
          "en": "So that's the first thing we want do before storing the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.46000000000001,
          "end": 108.72,
          "en": "in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.72,
          "end": 110.52000000000001,
          "en": "We create a password hash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "by calling hash and passing the raw password to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 117.47999999999999,
          "en": "And then as a second argument, the number of sold rounds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.47999999999999,
          "end": 121.35,
          "en": "which simply influences the strength of the hash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.35,
          "end": 123.3,
          "en": "Now hash is an asynchronous function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.3,
          "end": 126.003,
          "en": "returning a promise, hence we'll just a wait dis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.14,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "And then it's the password hash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 133.533,
          "en": "which we store in the database, not the plain password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 137.28,
          "en": "So that's how we should create a new user now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.28,
          "end": 140.13,
          "en": "And with that, we can now await this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.13,
          "end": 142.083,
          "en": "before we're done with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.01,
          "end": 145.77,
          "en": "Now we're not entirely done with everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.77,
          "end": 146.94,
          "en": "that should be added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.94,
          "end": 149.46,
          "en": "but we made an important step forward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.46,
          "end": 152.583,
          "en": "We are able to store users in the database now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.57,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "And therefore we can now go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "to our auth route and dare to the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 163.07999999999998,
          "en": "And here in this signup branch of this, if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "we can call this signup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 167.13,
          "en": "which we just worked on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 169.2,
          "en": "which is imported of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.2,
          "end": 173.073,
          "en": "from the auth dot server file in that data folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.94,
          "end": 177.3,
          "en": "And that signup function wants our credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.3,
          "end": 179.67000000000002,
          "en": "it wants an object with a email and a password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.67000000000002,
          "end": 182.733,
          "en": "and that is exactly what our credentials here are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.93,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "And it will return a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 187.38,
          "en": "so we should await that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.38,
          "end": 190.53,
          "en": "And then thereafter we can, for example, redirect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.53,
          "end": 194.763,
          "en": "to the starting page or to slash expenses for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 197.67000000000002,
          "en": "And redirect, of course is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.67000000000002,
          "end": 201.123,
          "en": "which is also imported from Remix run node again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 205.05,
          "en": "With that we do create users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.05,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "We still don't really create sessions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 210.03300000000002,
          "en": "but we are able to create users at least.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.9,
          "end": 214.26,
          "en": "But you might of course also recall that this could fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 214.26,
          "end": 217.2,
          "en": "This signup function could fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.2,
          "end": 218.46,
          "en": "If you take a look at it, again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.46,
          "end": 220.62,
          "en": "it fails if we have an existing user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.62,
          "end": 222.48,
          "en": "In that case, we throw our error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.48,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "with that status property set to 422.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 229.26,
          "en": "But first of all, before we handle this potential error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.26,
          "end": 230.85,
          "en": "of duplicate emails,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.85,
          "end": 233.43,
          "en": "let's try whether the current signup logic works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.43,
          "end": 234.78300000000002,
          "en": "with new users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.68,
          "end": 237.45,
          "en": "For that back on the auth page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.45,
          "end": 240.33,
          "en": "you should switch to the create a user mode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.33,
          "end": 243.81,
          "en": "and then enter a email address that hasn't been used yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.81,
          "end": 246.54,
          "en": "And here, since I haven't added any users at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.54,
          "end": 249.18,
          "en": "all email addresses are unused.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249.18,
          "end": 251.1,
          "en": "And if I create a user here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 251.1,
          "end": 254.43,
          "en": "I switch to that submitting mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.43,
          "end": 256.8,
          "en": "and then I'm forwarded to my expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.8,
          "end": 258.57,
          "en": "So that's looking good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.57,
          "end": 261,
          "en": "And if we now take a look at the user collection here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261,
          "end": 262.35,
          "en": "in mongo DB",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 262.35,
          "end": 264.51,
          "en": "we also see that a user was added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 264.51,
          "end": 267.57,
          "en": "And there we see that the password was hashed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 267.57,
          "end": 270.45,
          "en": "It's not the password I entered, it's not readable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 270.45,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "and that's exactly how it should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 275.323,
          "en": "So that's an important step forward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 275.323,
          "end": 279.12,
          "en": "Now if I enter a password that has been taken,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 279.12,
          "end": 281.55,
          "en": "so if I go back to that log in page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 281.55,
          "end": 286.353,
          "en": "and I create a user with that same password I just used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 288.87,
          "end": 291.15,
          "en": "then I get this default error page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 291.15,
          "end": 294.03,
          "en": "with my custom error message, that's great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 294.03,
          "end": 297.51,
          "en": "But this is of course not a great user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 297.51,
          "end": 300.03,
          "en": "Of course we tell the user what went wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 300.03,
          "end": 302.52,
          "en": "but if I just had a typo in my email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 302.52,
          "end": 305.37,
          "en": "I now have to go back, go back here, go back here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 305.37,
          "end": 307.32,
          "en": "and enter everything again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 307.32,
          "end": 309.363,
          "en": "That's not a good experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 310.44,
          "end": 313.95,
          "en": "And therefore I don't wanna let the Remix default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 313.95,
          "end": 315.87,
          "en": "error handler take over.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 315.87,
          "end": 319.53,
          "en": "But instead, I'll wrap this if check into a try catch block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 319.53,
          "end": 321.813,
          "en": "where I catch my potential error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 322.68,
          "end": 325.08,
          "en": "And I then wanna check in the catch block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 325.08,
          "end": 328.23,
          "en": "if the error object has a status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 328.23,
          "end": 330.6,
          "en": "that's set equal to 422,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 330.6,
          "end": 333.6,
          "en": "which is the status code I'm setting in my",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 333.6,
          "end": 335.913,
          "en": "auth dot server js file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 337.77,
          "end": 340.5,
          "en": "So if I have an error with that status property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 340.5,
          "end": 342.03,
          "en": "equal to 422,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 342.03,
          "end": 343.98,
          "en": "I know that it's this problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 343.98,
          "end": 347.64,
          "en": "or some other user input related problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 347.64,
          "end": 348.96,
          "en": "And in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 348.96,
          "end": 352.02,
          "en": "I'll return an object instead of throwing an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 352.02,
          "end": 354,
          "en": "And that object will have the same shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 354,
          "end": 358.56,
          "en": "as my object thrown by validate credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 358.56,
          "end": 360.9,
          "en": "Where I add some identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 360.9,
          "end": 363.78,
          "en": "I'll name it credentials here, but the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 363.78,
          "end": 366.24,
          "en": "And then some error message where I say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 366.24,
          "end": 369.03,
          "en": "could not authenticate user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 369.03,
          "end": 370.8,
          "en": "or better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 370.8,
          "end": 373.983,
          "en": "where we simply use the message encoded in the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 375,
          "end": 377.73,
          "en": "And with that, if we do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 377.73,
          "end": 381.27,
          "en": "and we then try creating an existing user again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 381.27,
          "end": 383.13,
          "en": "now I get the error message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 383.13,
          "end": 385.17,
          "en": "and I can simply fix my typo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 385.17,
          "end": 388.14,
          "en": "and create a new user successful thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 388.14,
          "end": 390.903,
          "en": "So that's now a much better user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
